1
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:05,399
MAN:
Police found her in the street.

2
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:08,151
Looks like she was bitten
by some kind of an animal.

3
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:12,489
WOMAN: Jesus. Her water's broken.
She's going into uterine contractions.

4
00:01:12,656 --> 00:01:14,199
We have to do a C-section.

5
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:32,134
[BABY CRYING]

6
00:01:32,301 --> 00:01:34,636
[EKG FLATLINING]

7
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:15,719
- What you got down there, little man?
- That's my heat-seeker.

8
00:02:15,886 --> 00:02:17,095
I'll bet it is.

9
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:19,306
[SQUEALS]

10
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:20,515
[LAUGHS]

11
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:23,727
- So where we going?
- It's a surprise, baby.

12
00:02:23,894 --> 00:02:28,065
Yeah, I like surprises. Yeah.

13
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:33,612
Oh, my God.

14
00:02:34,488 --> 00:02:36,323
What the fuck are we doing here?

15
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:40,702
Whoo. Look at all that.

16
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,621
[LAUGHS]

17
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:45,332
What the fuck is that?

18
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:52,923
Hey.

19
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:55,550
[SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

20
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,969
What did you just say?

21
00:03:06,395 --> 00:03:09,564
[DANCE MUSIC PLAYING]
OVER SPEAKERS]

22
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,259
Wow.

23
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:56,737
Hey, what's up? Oh, man.

24
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:08,457
Whoo! All right.

25
00:04:15,172 --> 00:04:18,800
Yeah. Whoo!

26
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,980
[LAUGHING]

27
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:35,108
What's happening?

28
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:37,110
[GRUNTS]

29
00:04:43,492 --> 00:04:44,618
Hey, man.

30
00:04:50,332 --> 00:04:52,000
Fuck.

31
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:04,429
Fuck, I need a drink.

32
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,228
No. No.

33
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:00,402
What's wrong, baby?

34
00:06:00,569 --> 00:06:01,862
[HISSES]

35
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:04,865
[SCREAMING]

36
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,408
No!

37
00:06:06,575 --> 00:06:08,910
[GROWLING AND HISSING]

38
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,414
Oh, no.

39
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:38,690
MAN 1:
Shut up, man.

40
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:00,420
WOMAN: Is that him?
MAN 2: Jesus, it's him.

41
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,214
MAN 3:
It's the Day Walker.

42
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:26,988
Come on, Day Walker!

43
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:29,115
[VAMPIRES SCREAMING]

44
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:33,620
[SCREAMING]

45
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:50,470
Hey! I'm gonna rip
your fucking head off.

46
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,490
- Look out! Hey, out of the way!
- Get out of there!

47
00:08:43,982 --> 00:08:47,819
That's him. That's him.
Get him. Fuck him up.

48
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:53,158
We're gonna jack you up.
Make him hurt bad. Whoo!

49
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:42,665
[YELLING]

50
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:49,380
[QUINN SPEAKING
IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

51
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:58,348
Quinn...

52
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:03,436
...I'm getting a little tired
of chopping you up.

53
00:10:07,357 --> 00:10:11,027
Thought I might try fire, for a change.

54
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,990
Give my regards to Frost.

55
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:21,871
No, please. Please don't.

56
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:23,957
MAN 1:
Over here, sergeant.

57
00:10:35,927 --> 00:10:37,262
- Put him out.
- Yes, sir.

58
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:39,514
MAN 2:
Paramedics, coming through.

59
00:11:01,995 --> 00:11:05,582
Got a charred cadaver here for you.
It's still warm too.

60
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,250
One, two, three.

61
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:15,175
Oh, Jesus, that's rank.

62
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:18,469
MAN: Paramedics said he was
still screaming when they found him...

63
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:21,097
...stapled to a wall.

64
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:23,516
CURTIS:
That's very pretty.

65
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:39,866
CURTIS: Did you check the chem panel?
Blood sugar's three times the norm.

66
00:11:40,033 --> 00:11:42,118
Phosphorus and uric acid
are off the charts.

67
00:11:42,285 --> 00:11:44,495
KAREN:
You took this off a DOA?

68
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:47,123
Yeah.

69
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,500
But this doesn't make any sense.

70
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:55,965
The red blood cells are biconvex,
which is impossible.

71
00:11:56,466 --> 00:11:59,344
Look at the polys, they're binucleated.

72
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:06,684
- Okay, Curtis, it's 3:00 in the morning...
- This is not a joke.

73
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:10,063
I've got the body sitting in the morgue
right now.

74
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:13,733
I thought you promised
to give me some distance.

75
00:12:14,317 --> 00:12:16,486
I just want you to come down
and take a look.

76
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:26,663
Okay. Show me the body.

77
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:28,998
And I don't wanna hear
a word about us.

78
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:32,543
Done. We've had that conversation.

79
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:38,091
You haven't started
on the internal organs yet?

80
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:41,386
No, just a blood sample
through the pericardium.

81
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:46,015
The maxilla looks a little deformed.

82
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:48,685
There's some odd muscle structure
around the canines.

83
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:51,854
I'm gonna go ahead start the Y
and check the tracheal mucosa.

84
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:59,279
Let me ask you something.

85
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:02,073
Honestly.

86
00:13:02,824 --> 00:13:05,368
You ever have second thoughts
about us?

87
00:13:07,704 --> 00:13:08,788
Sometimes.

88
00:13:10,957 --> 00:13:13,543
But then I remember
how much of an asshole you were.

89
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:15,336
You wanna cut me some slack here?

90
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:18,089
You asked for some time off,
I gave you some time off.

91
00:13:18,256 --> 00:13:20,550
- Look, Curtis, it's over.
- I'm trying. Really, I am.

92
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:22,468
[GASPING]

93
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:43,698
MAN 1: Call security!
MAN 2: Get back!

94
00:13:58,629 --> 00:14:00,298
Came back to finish you off.

95
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:02,342
Get out of my way, you freak.

96
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,892
Freeze!

97
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:15,480
Motherfucker,
are you out of your damn mind?

98
00:14:24,572 --> 00:14:26,991
[SCREAMING]

99
00:15:05,947 --> 00:15:07,782
MAN 1: He's there, right there.
MAN 2: Go ahead.

100
00:15:07,949 --> 00:15:09,450
- Go.
MAN 3: Hey, you, freeze.

101
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,035
MAN 4: Come on. Come on.
MAN 5: Fire.

102
00:15:12,495 --> 00:15:13,704
MAN 6:
Keep going. Keep going.

103
00:15:16,541 --> 00:15:18,376
MAN 7:
Come back out.

104
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:21,254
MAN 3: Go.
MAN 7: He can't get out.

105
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:24,424
[SCREAMING]

106
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:30,430
- Freeze!
MAN 1: Hold it right there.

107
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:32,640
MAN 2: Don't do it.
MAN 3: Hey, hey...

108
00:15:46,404 --> 00:15:48,030
KAREN:
My shoulder...

109
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:50,700
...is dislocated.

110
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,036
[YELLS]

111
00:17:34,595 --> 00:17:36,973
[MACHINERY BUZZING]

112
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:39,433
[OVER SPEAKERS]
<i>I feel rivers overflowing</i>

113
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,435
BLADE:
Whistler.

114
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,982
Whistler.

115
00:17:48,109 --> 00:17:49,777
[MUSIC STOPS]

116
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:53,489
WHISTLER:
Bringing home strays now?

117
00:17:55,992 --> 00:17:57,201
She's been bitten.

118
00:18:01,581 --> 00:18:03,291
Should've killed her, then.

119
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,418
Yeah, I know...

120
00:18:07,295 --> 00:18:08,838
...but I didn't.

121
00:18:15,595 --> 00:18:20,850
You watch her close.
She starts to turn, you finish her off.

122
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:26,772
Or I will.

123
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:35,489
She's borderline.

124
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:40,953
Another hour,
she'd be well into the change.

125
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:46,125
Dr. Karen Jenson, listen close.

126
00:18:46,459 --> 00:18:50,838
I'm gonna inject you
with allium sativum. Garlic.

127
00:18:51,005 --> 00:18:53,007
This is gonna hurt a lot.

128
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:55,051
It was Quinn.

129
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:57,762
Frost's little errand boy?

130
00:18:58,262 --> 00:19:00,890
- You get a lead on him?
- No.

131
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,559
WHISTLER:
Too bad.

132
00:19:05,186 --> 00:19:06,228
[GRUNTS]

133
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:08,272
Hold her.

134
00:19:18,449 --> 00:19:23,162
I give her fifty-fifty,
if she makes it through the night.

135
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:52,900
Blade, the Day Walker.

136
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:55,611
Still pursuing his ridiculous crusade.

137
00:19:59,407 --> 00:20:01,450
How many died?

138
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:06,580
We don't have an exact count.
Apparently, he used a lot of silver.

139
00:20:07,373 --> 00:20:10,167
- We're having difficulty...
- Send in Frost.

140
00:20:18,509 --> 00:20:19,635
Deacon Frost.

141
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:25,891
You can come in now.

142
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:39,196
[IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

143
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:01,927
These nightclubs of yours
are dangerous.

144
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:03,763
Are they?

145
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:07,558
They draw needless attention
to our kind. You know our policy.

146
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:09,727
Your policy, not mine.

147
00:21:10,311 --> 00:21:11,896
DRAGONETTI:
Our livelihood...

148
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:16,901
...depends on our ability to blend in...

149
00:21:17,151 --> 00:21:18,527
...on our discretion.

150
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:22,782
Maybe it's time
we forgot about discretion.

151
00:21:23,491 --> 00:21:25,201
We should be ruling the humans...

152
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:28,329
...not running around
making back-alley treaties with them.

153
00:21:28,496 --> 00:21:31,957
For fuck's sake,
these people are our food not our allies.

154
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:34,877
- You're out of line, Frost.
- Am I?

155
00:21:35,044 --> 00:21:38,756
Maybe I'm just the first to say out loud
what we've all been thinking.

156
00:21:38,923 --> 00:21:43,469
We have existed this way
for thousands of years.

157
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:48,224
Who are you to challenge our ways?

158
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:50,559
You're not even a pureblood.

159
00:21:53,938 --> 00:21:55,189
Like it matters.

160
00:21:56,440 --> 00:22:00,152
I was born a vampire...

161
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:04,031
...as was every other member
of this house.

162
00:22:04,198 --> 00:22:05,366
But, you, Frost...

163
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:11,413
...you were merely turned.

164
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:17,503
The world belongs to us,
not the humans.

165
00:22:17,837 --> 00:22:20,005
You know that.

166
00:22:23,968 --> 00:22:26,804
Do we have any other business
to discuss?

167
00:22:27,638 --> 00:22:31,976
Well, there's the matter of our offshore
accounts. We're having difficulty...

168
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:33,769
And have you made the transfer...?

169
00:22:33,936 --> 00:22:39,233
Gaetano, you may wake up one day
and find yourself extinct.

170
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:52,621
[BELL RINGS]

171
00:23:12,349 --> 00:23:15,978
- You're a week early.
- Yeah.

172
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:26,780
Whistler says I'm building up
a resistance to the serum.

173
00:23:28,616 --> 00:23:31,076
Yeah, I figured that might happen.

174
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:42,546
You take care, all right?

175
00:25:26,734 --> 00:25:29,319
WHISTLER: I must be getting soft
in my old age...

176
00:25:29,486 --> 00:25:32,322
...letting you bring home
a stray like that.

177
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:37,911
It was damn stupid of you.
You might have lucked out though.

178
00:25:38,871 --> 00:25:41,165
I checked her background.

179
00:25:43,834 --> 00:25:47,087
Turns out she's a hematologist.

180
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:50,549
She might be useful to us.

181
00:25:51,467 --> 00:25:53,343
BLADE:
I doubt it.

182
00:25:54,386 --> 00:25:55,971
WHISTLER:
I'm serious.

183
00:25:56,138 --> 00:26:01,143
I took a look at that notebook of hers.
She's on to something.

184
00:26:03,062 --> 00:26:04,563
I had to increase the dose.

185
00:26:06,065 --> 00:26:09,401
It's over 50 milligrams now.
That's getting dangerous.

186
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:14,031
Just do it, old man.

187
00:27:13,549 --> 00:27:15,551
Wander off the beaten path, doctor?

188
00:27:17,427 --> 00:27:19,263
Who are you people?

189
00:27:19,429 --> 00:27:20,848
My name's Abraham Whistler.

190
00:27:22,266 --> 00:27:23,600
You've met Blade.

191
00:27:39,825 --> 00:27:41,660
So am I a prisoner here?

192
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:45,080
Not at all.

193
00:27:45,247 --> 00:27:49,418
We just had to take certain precautions
before we let you go.

194
00:27:49,877 --> 00:27:52,838
You gotta understand,
they're everywhere.

195
00:27:53,005 --> 00:27:54,840
Vampires.

196
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:56,633
The <i>Hominis nocturna.</i>

197
00:27:57,885 --> 00:27:59,469
We hunt them, you see.

198
00:27:59,636 --> 00:28:03,223
Moving from one city to the next
tracking their migrations.

199
00:28:03,390 --> 00:28:04,641
They're hard to kill.

200
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:08,395
- They tend to regenerate.
- And I'm supposed to believe all this?

201
00:28:08,562 --> 00:28:11,565
Well, you already met Mr. Crispy
at the hospital.

202
00:28:11,732 --> 00:28:13,317
What do you think?

203
00:28:15,777 --> 00:28:19,239
So, what do you use, then?
Stakes? Crosses?

204
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:24,119
Crosses don't do squat.
Some of the legends are true, though.

205
00:28:24,286 --> 00:28:27,998
Vampires are severely allergic to silver.

206
00:28:28,165 --> 00:28:30,959
Feed them garlic
and they go into anaphylactic shock.

207
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:34,463
Then, of course, there's always sunlight,
ultraviolet rays.

208
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:40,135
I got this sucker running.
You wanna give it a try tonight?

209
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:47,559
Still heavy.

210
00:28:48,936 --> 00:28:50,395
But you're so big.

211
00:28:52,898 --> 00:28:56,401
If you wanna live to see another day,
you'll be out of town by nightfall.

212
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:58,320
So where am I supposed to go?

213
00:29:02,115 --> 00:29:04,618
You've been exposed to them.

214
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:08,538
One way or another,
somebody's gonna take you out.

215
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:15,462
There's a war going on out there.

216
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:18,757
Blade, myself, a few others...

217
00:29:18,924 --> 00:29:22,010
...we've tried to keep it
from spilling over onto the streets...

218
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:26,515
...but sometimes, people like yourself
get caught in the crossfire.

219
00:29:26,682 --> 00:29:29,309
I have blood samples.
I can go to the police.

220
00:29:29,476 --> 00:29:31,937
They own the police.

221
00:29:32,104 --> 00:29:34,606
You have to understand,
they're everywhere.

222
00:29:34,773 --> 00:29:37,484
Chances are you've seen them yourself
and didn't know it.

223
00:29:37,651 --> 00:29:39,361
On the subway or in a bar.

224
00:29:41,655 --> 00:29:43,573
So that's it?

225
00:29:44,533 --> 00:29:47,411
You guys just patch me up
and send me on my way.

226
00:29:51,415 --> 00:29:55,377
Here. Vampire Mace.

227
00:29:56,295 --> 00:29:58,255
Silver nitrate, essence of garlic.

228
00:29:59,172 --> 00:30:00,966
You keep your eyes open.

229
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:03,468
Be careful.

230
00:30:06,972 --> 00:30:09,224
One other thing...

231
00:30:09,725 --> 00:30:12,185
...buy yourself a gun.

232
00:30:12,894 --> 00:30:15,147
If you start getting sensitive
to daylight...

233
00:30:16,481 --> 00:30:21,486
...if you find you're thirsty, regardless
of how much you've had to drink...

234
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:25,866
...then I suggest you take that gun
and use it on yourself.

235
00:30:29,036 --> 00:30:31,955
Better that than the alternative.

236
00:31:27,219 --> 00:31:29,137
[DANCE MUSIC PLAYING
ON HEADPHONES]

237
00:31:29,304 --> 00:31:31,306
You have been warned before.

238
00:31:31,473 --> 00:31:35,936
These archives are restricted
to the members of the House of Erebus.

239
00:31:37,938 --> 00:31:41,900
You are wasting your time.
It's a dead language.

240
00:31:42,067 --> 00:31:45,654
The ancient texts
can never be translated.

241
00:31:47,114 --> 00:31:49,282
You wouldn't even understand them.

242
00:31:51,743 --> 00:31:53,954
Damn it, Frost, I'm talking to you!

243
00:31:54,955 --> 00:31:57,833
Shh.

244
00:31:57,999 --> 00:32:00,877
Keep your voice down, Gaetano.

245
00:32:01,044 --> 00:32:02,295
[MUSIC STOPS]

246
00:32:02,462 --> 00:32:05,090
We're in a library.
You don't need to shout.

247
00:32:06,550 --> 00:32:08,885
What are you up to, Frost?

248
00:32:20,188 --> 00:32:23,108
What are you gonna do? Hm?

249
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,656
What?

250
00:32:34,244 --> 00:32:36,496
You bore me.

251
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:13,783
BLADE:
Remember what we told you.

252
00:33:13,950 --> 00:33:17,162
You keep your eyes open.
They're everywhere.

253
00:33:19,122 --> 00:33:20,665
But it's daytime.

254
00:33:27,255 --> 00:33:29,591
MAN 1: Hey, hey, hey, that's mine.
MAN 2: Spare some change?

