498
00:58:11,196 --> 00:58:15,534
<i>He'd been living on the streets,
feeding off the homeless.</i>

499
00:58:15,993 --> 00:58:19,204
<i>His need for blood
had taken hold at puberty.</i>

500
00:58:19,746 --> 00:58:22,916
I took him for a vampire at first.

501
00:58:23,208 --> 00:58:25,544
Almost killed him too.

502
00:58:25,711 --> 00:58:28,422
Then I realized what he was.

503
00:58:28,964 --> 00:58:32,884
Blade's mother was attacked
by a vampire while she was pregnant.

504
00:58:33,051 --> 00:58:36,054
She died, but he lived.

505
00:58:36,304 --> 00:58:39,975
Unfortunately,
he'd undergone certain genetic changes.

506
00:58:40,517 --> 00:58:45,564
He can withstand garlic, silver,
even sunlight.

507
00:58:45,731 --> 00:58:47,274
And he's got their strength.

508
00:58:49,359 --> 00:58:52,237
This time tomorrow,
all those wounds of his will be healed.

509
00:58:54,197 --> 00:58:56,700
He still ages like a human, though.

510
00:58:56,867 --> 00:58:59,411
See, vampires age slower than us.

511
00:59:00,620 --> 00:59:05,834
Unfortunately,
he also inherited their thirst.

512
00:59:06,418 --> 00:59:09,463
KAREN: I thought the serum
was supposed to suppress that.

513
00:59:09,629 --> 00:59:11,882
Time's running out.

514
00:59:13,258 --> 00:59:16,136
His body's starting to reject it.

515
00:59:16,762 --> 00:59:21,516
So far, all my efforts
to find a cure have failed.

516
00:59:25,395 --> 00:59:27,105
Why do you hunt them?

517
00:59:29,191 --> 00:59:31,610
I had a family once.

518
00:59:31,777 --> 00:59:34,946
A wife, two daughters.

519
00:59:36,782 --> 00:59:40,494
Then a drifter came calling one evening.
A vampire.

520
00:59:42,496 --> 00:59:44,289
He toyed with them first.

521
00:59:45,165 --> 00:59:49,086
Tried to make me decide
which order they'd die in.

522
00:59:52,798 --> 00:59:57,677
We kill as many of them as we can find,
but it's getting worse.

523
00:59:57,844 --> 00:59:59,096
Because of Frost.

524
00:59:59,262 --> 01:00:02,682
There's something happening
in the vampire ranks.

525
01:00:02,849 --> 01:00:05,018
It's something big.

526
01:00:05,310 --> 01:00:09,731
And I'd stake my life
that son of a bitch is at the center of it.

527
01:00:13,318 --> 01:00:15,362
KAREN:
Blade?

528
01:00:32,337 --> 01:00:35,215
Whistler told me what happened.

529
01:00:37,926 --> 01:00:40,762
He told me what you are.

530
01:00:43,515 --> 01:00:45,725
You don't know me.

531
01:00:45,892 --> 01:00:48,687
You don't know anything about me.

532
01:00:51,022 --> 01:00:53,066
I'm not human.

533
01:00:56,361 --> 01:00:57,404
You look human to me...

534
01:00:57,571 --> 01:01:00,365
Humans don't drink blood.

535
01:01:00,532 --> 01:01:02,951
That was a long time ago.

536
01:01:03,785 --> 01:01:05,912
Maybe you should let that go.

537
01:01:08,748 --> 01:01:13,670
I have spent my whole life looking
for that thing that killed my mother...

538
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:17,424
...and made me what I am.

539
01:01:19,926 --> 01:01:22,804
And every time
I take one of those monsters out...

540
01:01:22,971 --> 01:01:26,183
...I get a little piece of that life back.

541
01:01:26,349 --> 01:01:29,853
So don't you tell me about forgetting.

542
01:01:33,231 --> 01:01:34,733
QUINN:
My fault? He took us by surprise!

543
01:01:34,900 --> 01:01:37,652
Two of them against
your entire security force?

544
01:01:37,819 --> 01:01:40,030
Don't put that shit on me,
you were there too.

545
01:01:40,197 --> 01:01:43,325
I'm sure Deacon will appreciate
our cutback in payroll.

546
01:01:43,491 --> 01:01:46,703
QUINN: Ow! You little skeez.
- The amputee lifestyle really suits you.

547
01:01:46,870 --> 01:01:48,914
I should put this stump
through that grin.

548
01:01:49,080 --> 01:01:52,542
Face it, angel. You were sloppy.
You got what you deserved.

549
01:01:56,963 --> 01:01:58,882
QUINN:
Deac, let me take this guy out, man.

550
01:01:59,049 --> 01:02:01,468
Look what he fucking did!
He took my hand again!

551
01:02:01,635 --> 01:02:04,304
Listen to me. I want him alive.

552
01:02:04,471 --> 01:02:06,223
QUINN:
What the fuck are you talk...?

553
01:02:06,389 --> 01:02:09,559
You want him alive? We've been trying
to kill this motherfucker for years.

554
01:02:09,726 --> 01:02:11,478
Are you out of your fucking mind?
You want...?

555
01:02:11,645 --> 01:02:16,358
Shh. Big guy, relax.

556
01:02:16,524 --> 01:02:17,817
Be patient.

557
01:02:19,486 --> 01:02:20,946
We got a lot to do here.

558
01:02:22,405 --> 01:02:23,490
I need you, man.

559
01:02:27,452 --> 01:02:30,205
- I need you.
- Yeah.

560
01:03:12,664 --> 01:03:14,749
FROST:
Good morning.

561
01:03:15,417 --> 01:03:17,544
How you feeling?

562
01:03:26,261 --> 01:03:28,221
Look at that.

563
01:03:31,099 --> 01:03:34,769
Ooh! Getting a little toasty
out here, huh?

564
01:03:36,187 --> 01:03:40,108
When was the last time you stopped
to appreciate a good sunrise?

565
01:03:40,317 --> 01:03:44,362
That's right, you were born a vampire,
so you never had the pleasure, have you?

566
01:03:44,529 --> 01:03:47,407
That's okay. It's all right.

567
01:03:47,574 --> 01:03:50,785
At least we're here together.
Share the moment.

568
01:03:50,952 --> 01:03:53,538
Which means a lot to me
by the way, really.

569
01:03:53,705 --> 01:03:55,582
I mean that.

570
01:03:57,167 --> 01:03:59,461
Because actually,
when you get to know me...

571
01:03:59,627 --> 01:04:02,422
...I'm a fairly sentimental type of guy.

572
01:04:02,589 --> 01:04:05,383
Bit of an innocent, you might say.

573
01:04:07,177 --> 01:04:09,888
Do what you want, Frost.

574
01:04:10,221 --> 01:04:12,182
Doesn't make any difference.

575
01:04:13,600 --> 01:04:16,561
You just don't fucking get it.

576
01:04:17,896 --> 01:04:20,899
- You're never gonna be a pureblood.
- Hold him.

577
01:04:23,651 --> 01:04:25,945
DRAGONETTI:
You will never rule us.

578
01:04:27,238 --> 01:04:29,866
[DRAGONETTI GROANING]

579
01:04:38,375 --> 01:04:41,628
Jesus Christ. Have a nice day.

580
01:04:42,337 --> 01:04:45,382
Sorry, you old dog. You just got
a little too long in the teeth.

581
01:04:45,548 --> 01:04:46,925
[LAUGHING]

582
01:04:47,092 --> 01:04:51,763
What, man? That was funny.
"Long, tooth." It's funny, man.

583
01:04:51,930 --> 01:04:54,432
Did I tell you the one
about the leprechaun...?

584
01:04:58,144 --> 01:04:59,938
[SCREAMING]

585
01:05:23,253 --> 01:05:25,839
What have you done with Dragonetti?

586
01:05:32,429 --> 01:05:34,889
Let's get down to business, shall we?

587
01:05:35,056 --> 01:05:37,934
I need 12 volunteers.

588
01:05:44,524 --> 01:05:46,401
BLADE:
Whistler.

589
01:05:48,862 --> 01:05:50,155
WHISTLER:
What is this?

590
01:05:51,781 --> 01:05:54,367
Smells like a vampire
wiped his ass with it.

591
01:05:54,534 --> 01:05:55,952
I took it from the archives.

592
01:05:56,119 --> 01:05:58,955
WHISTLER: It's written in blood.
BLADE: It's from the Book of Erebus.

593
01:06:05,295 --> 01:06:07,672
I think it's what Frost
has been working on.

594
01:06:07,839 --> 01:06:11,217
WHISTLER: It's something about
the blood god, the Spirits of the 12.

595
01:06:11,384 --> 01:06:13,761
I don't know.
I can't make out the rest of it.

596
01:06:13,928 --> 01:06:15,472
Well, maybe this'll help.

597
01:06:16,389 --> 01:06:18,683
We'll figure out something.

598
01:06:19,392 --> 01:06:20,935
BLADE:
So, what's all of this?

599
01:06:21,102 --> 01:06:25,565
Took a trip to the hospital last night,
borrowed some equipment.

600
01:06:25,857 --> 01:06:28,526
For your miracle cure?

601
01:06:30,195 --> 01:06:32,947
KAREN:
This is EDTA. It's an anticoagulant.

602
01:06:33,114 --> 01:06:35,200
We use it to treat blood clots.

603
01:06:36,242 --> 01:06:40,538
Look what happens when I introduce it
onto a sample of vampire blood.

604
01:06:42,248 --> 01:06:44,209
Take a step back.

605
01:06:44,375 --> 01:06:47,086
The reaction's energetic.

606
01:06:55,512 --> 01:06:59,516
- Some cure.
KAREN: I didn't say EDTA was a cure.

607
01:06:59,682 --> 01:07:04,187
But maybe you could use it
to explode some vampire heads.

608
01:07:06,147 --> 01:07:08,900
Wait a minute.
I need a sample of your blood.

609
01:07:09,067 --> 01:07:12,612
Later. I gotta go downtown.

610
01:07:12,779 --> 01:07:15,490
- I need some serum.
WHISTLER: Serum can wait.

611
01:07:15,657 --> 01:07:18,034
This is important.

612
01:07:22,413 --> 01:07:24,207
[COUGHING]

613
01:07:39,055 --> 01:07:42,016
- Is he sick?
- Cancer.

614
01:07:44,727 --> 01:07:47,438
You have a lot of love for him,
don't you?

615
01:07:47,605 --> 01:07:52,569
We have a good arrangement.
He makes the weapons, I use them.

616
01:07:56,489 --> 01:08:00,994
You know, my mother used to say,
"A cold heart is a dead heart."

617
01:08:18,761 --> 01:08:21,139
You don't look so good.

618
01:08:21,723 --> 01:08:27,228
I'm just a little tired.
You know, we've been working all night.

619
01:08:29,314 --> 01:08:32,275
I guess we didn't catch it in time.

620
01:08:33,192 --> 01:08:37,447
You got another day, two at the most.

621
01:08:41,242 --> 01:08:43,536
For what it's worth, I'm sorry.

622
01:08:44,454 --> 01:08:47,624
You make it sound like
I'm already dead.

623
01:09:05,433 --> 01:09:07,268
FROST:
Blade.

624
01:09:31,125 --> 01:09:32,960
How you doing, chief?

625
01:09:34,420 --> 01:09:36,172
Easy.

626
01:09:37,131 --> 01:09:39,008
Wouldn't want our little friend here...

627
01:09:39,175 --> 01:09:41,886
...to wind up on the back
of a milk carton, would we?

628
01:09:44,430 --> 01:09:48,893
It's nice to finally meet you, man.
Had my eye on you for years.

629
01:09:49,060 --> 01:09:54,065
I know all about you.
Your serum, Whistler, everything.

630
01:09:54,565 --> 01:09:56,067
Sunblock.

631
01:09:56,234 --> 01:09:58,528
Hey, it's a start, right?

632
01:09:58,695 --> 01:10:02,281
The goal, of course, is to be like you.
A Day Walker.

633
01:10:03,866 --> 01:10:05,952
You got the best of both worlds,
don't you?

634
01:10:06,911 --> 01:10:09,997
All our strengths,
none of our weaknesses.

635
01:10:10,790 --> 01:10:13,126
Well, maybe I don't see it that way.

636
01:10:13,292 --> 01:10:16,170
Oh, so it's back to pretending
we're human again?

637
01:10:16,337 --> 01:10:19,882
Come on.
Spare me the Uncle Tom routine, okay?

638
01:10:20,049 --> 01:10:23,136
You can't keep denying
what you are, man.

639
01:10:23,928 --> 01:10:28,141
You think the humans will ever accept
a half-breed like you? They can't.

640
01:10:28,307 --> 01:10:30,435
They're afraid of you.

641
01:10:30,601 --> 01:10:33,312
And they should be. You're an animal.

642
01:10:33,479 --> 01:10:35,356
You're a fucking maniac.

643
01:10:39,110 --> 01:10:42,196
Look at them. They're cattle.

644
01:10:42,363 --> 01:10:44,198
Pieces of meat.

645
01:10:44,365 --> 01:10:47,160
What difference does it make
how their world ends?

646
01:10:47,326 --> 01:10:51,539
Plague, war, famine.

647
01:10:51,706 --> 01:10:54,917
Morality doesn't even enter into it.

648
01:10:55,084 --> 01:10:59,964
We're just a function
of natural selection, man. The new race.

649
01:11:00,673 --> 01:11:03,134
Looks like your mascara's running.

650
01:11:10,475 --> 01:11:14,270
I'm offering you a truce.
I want you with us.

651
01:11:14,437 --> 01:11:17,190
What, do you think I'm stupid?

652
01:11:18,024 --> 01:11:19,859
[IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

653
01:11:25,072 --> 01:11:26,908
You're familiar with the blood god.

654
01:11:27,074 --> 01:11:29,285
[IN ENGLISH]
Frost...

655
01:11:29,702 --> 01:11:32,288
...you're nothing to me...

656
01:11:32,455 --> 01:11:35,333
...but another dead vampire.

657
01:11:35,500 --> 01:11:38,085
You're an idiot, you know that?

658
01:11:38,252 --> 01:11:40,546
I came down here
offering you an easy way out...

659
01:11:40,713 --> 01:11:43,925
...and you spit it right back
in my fucking face.

660
01:11:44,842 --> 01:11:46,552
Careful.

661
01:11:50,264 --> 01:11:52,517
What do I care?

662
01:11:52,683 --> 01:11:56,771
They're nothing but cattle,
just like you said.

663
01:11:57,313 --> 01:12:00,483
If you wanna take the hard road,
be my guest, pal.

664
01:12:00,650 --> 01:12:02,902
But I promise you,
by the time this is over...

665
01:12:03,069 --> 01:12:06,572
...you're gonna wish they never cut you
from your mother's womb.

666
01:12:15,498 --> 01:12:17,291
[SCREAMING]

667
01:12:40,648 --> 01:12:41,941
Go home.

668
01:12:45,820 --> 01:12:48,364
It's simple.
Why do vampires need to drink blood?

669
01:12:48,531 --> 01:12:51,200
Because their own blood
can't sustain hemoglobin.

670
01:12:51,367 --> 01:12:54,287
Right. So it's a genetic defect
just like hemolytic anemia.

671
01:12:54,453 --> 01:12:57,081
That means that we have to treat it
with gene therapy.

672
01:12:57,248 --> 01:13:00,793
Rewrite the victim's DNA
with a retrovirus.

673
01:13:00,960 --> 01:13:03,045
They've been using it
on sickle-cell anemia.

674
01:13:03,212 --> 01:13:04,422
Are you sure that's safe?

675
01:13:04,589 --> 01:13:08,801
I have no idea,
but I don't have a choice, do I?

676
01:13:10,970 --> 01:13:12,763
You actually think this could work?

677
01:13:12,930 --> 01:13:16,684
On me? Yes.

678
01:13:16,934 --> 01:13:18,769
On Blade, I'm not so sure.

679
01:13:18,936 --> 01:13:22,356
See, he didn't contract vampirism
from a bite like I did.

680
01:13:22,523 --> 01:13:26,319
He was born with it.
It's part of his DNA.

681
01:13:27,403 --> 01:13:30,907
I'm sure I can cure his thirst,
but it's gonna take time.

682
01:13:31,073 --> 01:13:33,534
We're out of time.

683
01:13:33,701 --> 01:13:36,412
You saw what was on that disk.

684
01:13:36,621 --> 01:13:38,998
[QUINN LAUGHING]

685
01:13:41,083 --> 01:13:43,002
Damn.

686
01:13:43,961 --> 01:13:45,546
Get out of here.

687
01:14:01,354 --> 01:14:02,855
[YELLS]

688
01:14:10,655 --> 01:14:12,198
I said, get out of here.

689
01:14:18,287 --> 01:14:21,707
Nice place. Took us a while to find it.

690
01:14:30,007 --> 01:14:32,802
- Bite me and get it over with.
- I ain't gonna bite you.

691
01:14:46,315 --> 01:14:48,359
Do your thing.

692
01:15:00,162 --> 01:15:02,039
Whistler?

693
01:16:09,065 --> 01:16:10,900
Frost took her.

694
01:16:18,699 --> 01:16:20,868
Listen to me.

695
01:16:23,245 --> 01:16:25,372
The disk...

696
01:16:25,623 --> 01:16:27,208
...we decoded it.

697
01:16:27,708 --> 01:16:33,964
Frost is trying to trigger
a fucking vampire apocalypse.

698
01:16:36,175 --> 01:16:38,511
There's some kind of...

699
01:16:38,803 --> 01:16:42,681
...vampire god he's trying to resurrect.

700
01:16:43,474 --> 01:16:44,934
La Magra.

701
01:16:48,479 --> 01:16:50,898
You're the key.

702
01:16:51,816 --> 01:16:53,400
He needs your blood.

703
01:16:57,154 --> 01:16:59,949
The blood of the Day Walker.

704
01:17:02,243 --> 01:17:04,495
You're the chosen one.

705
01:17:08,082 --> 01:17:10,417
Listen to me, Blade.

706
01:17:11,252 --> 01:17:14,547
- You can't go after him.
- Bullshit.

707
01:17:14,713 --> 01:17:20,010
If Frost gets his hands on you,
it's all over.

708
01:17:22,304 --> 01:17:25,391
There'll be armies
of the motherfuckers.

709
01:17:27,685 --> 01:17:29,812
Shit.

710
01:17:33,732 --> 01:17:35,442
You're gonna have to finish me off.

711
01:17:37,111 --> 01:17:39,738
Don't want me coming back.

712
01:17:41,073 --> 01:17:42,658
We can treat the wounds.

713
01:17:44,451 --> 01:17:46,036
It's too far gone.

714
01:17:46,954 --> 01:17:49,331
You know that.

715
01:17:52,042 --> 01:17:54,211
Give me your gun.

716
01:17:56,088 --> 01:17:57,423
No.

717
01:17:58,799 --> 01:18:01,135
Give me the goddamn gun.

718
01:18:26,243 --> 01:18:29,914
Now walk away,
you stupid son of a bitch.

719
01:18:34,752 --> 01:18:37,087
Walk the fuck away.

720
01:18:46,305 --> 01:18:48,265
[GUNSHOT]

721
01:18:58,192 --> 01:19:01,779
<i>By the time you watch this,
your friend Whistler should be dead.</i>

722
01:19:01,946 --> 01:19:05,157
<i>If it makes any difference to you,
he put up quite a fight.</i>

723
01:19:05,449 --> 01:19:08,535
<i>You can find us
at the Edgewood Towers.</i>

724
01:20:46,133 --> 01:20:48,552
You seem a bit tense.

725
01:20:48,719 --> 01:20:51,972
A bit pent-up maybe,
like you need to release something.

726
01:20:53,557 --> 01:20:58,812
No?
Blade not... giving it to you maybe?

727
01:21:00,064 --> 01:21:02,024
I don't know, I just...

728
01:21:02,566 --> 01:21:05,235
I see such a beautiful woman.

729
01:21:06,153 --> 01:21:08,405
Great skin.

730
01:21:10,282 --> 01:21:12,117
I'd like to see you happy, that's all.

731
01:21:12,284 --> 01:21:16,288
Is this the part
where you offer to turn me?

732
01:21:17,039 --> 01:21:19,500
Well, it's either that or a body bag.

733
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:22,795
Go ahead. Bite me.

734
01:21:23,629 --> 01:21:25,798
I'll just cure myself.

735
01:21:25,964 --> 01:21:28,967
I did it before, and I can do it again.

736
01:21:29,134 --> 01:21:33,138
- There is no cure, baby.
- There is if you've been bitten.

737
01:21:33,514 --> 01:21:35,808
If you were once human.

738
01:21:41,230 --> 01:21:43,732
How'd you get that scar, Deacon?

739
01:21:43,899 --> 01:21:46,985
A born vampire would have the power
to regenerate from birth.

740
01:21:47,152 --> 01:21:50,197
You must've gotten scarred
before you were turned.

741
01:21:51,031 --> 01:21:52,699
Isn't that right?

742
01:21:52,866 --> 01:21:55,411
Vampires like you aren't a species.

743
01:21:55,577 --> 01:21:59,832
You're just infected, a virus,
a sexually-transmitted disease...

744
01:21:59,998 --> 01:22:02,126
I'll tell you what we are, sister.

745
01:22:02,292 --> 01:22:05,754
We're the top of the fucking food chain.
The blood god's coming...

746
01:22:05,921 --> 01:22:09,758
...and after tonight,
you people are fucking history.

747
01:22:09,925 --> 01:22:13,554
He's a hurricane, an act of God.

748
01:22:13,720 --> 01:22:16,306
Anyone caught in his path
will instantly be turned.

749
01:22:18,350 --> 01:22:20,185
Everyone you've ever known...

750
01:22:20,352 --> 01:22:23,647
...everyone you've ever fucking loved.

751
01:22:23,814 --> 01:22:27,109
It won't matter who's pureblood
and who's not.

752
01:22:27,818 --> 01:22:30,737
How you gonna cure
the whole fucking world?

753
01:22:36,452 --> 01:22:38,829
And Blade's blood is the key.

754
01:22:39,163 --> 01:22:40,622
We've got an intruder.

755
01:22:52,384 --> 01:22:54,052
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

756
01:22:54,219 --> 01:22:57,097
[MOTOR REVVING]

757
01:23:08,525 --> 01:23:09,818
